<figure class="flex flex-col gap-4 border-2 border-ink p-4 sm:p-6">
<p class="font-bold">The ladder and barn are measured differently in two frames.</p>
<svg viewBox="0 0 480 245" class="w-full" role="img" aria-labelledby="ladder-fig-title ladder-fig-desc">
<title id="ladder-fig-title">The ladder fits in the barn frame but not in its own</title>
<desc id="ladder-fig-desc">Top: in the barn frame, a 10 metre ladder fits in a 12 metre barn. Bottom: in the ladder frame, the ladder is 20 metres and the barn is 6 metres. Door closing times also differ between the frames.</desc>
<g fill="currentColor" font-size="17" font-family="sans-serif">
<text x="20" y="28">Barn’s frame</text><text x="20" y="145">Ladder’s frame</text>
<text x="155" y="60">Barn: 12 m</text><text x="165" y="106">Ladder: 10 m</text>
<text x="190" y="174">Ladder: 20 m</text><text x="190" y="218">Barn: 6 m</text>
</g>
<rect x="105" y="68" width="300" height="36" fill="#d7a13d" fill-opacity=".25" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/>
<rect x="130" y="81" width="250" height="11" fill="#387a91"/>
<rect x="105" y="182" width="90" height="36" fill="#d7a13d" fill-opacity=".25" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/>
<rect x="105" y="195" width="300" height="11" fill="#387a91"/>
</svg>
<figcaption class="text-base leading-normal">At about 0.87 times light speed, the ladder is 10 m in the barn’s frame and fits in its 12 m barn. In the ladder’s frame, the barn is just 6 m and the ladder stays 20 m. The missing piece is timing: the two doors are not closed simultaneously in the ladder’s frame. Bar lengths compare objects <strong>within</strong> each frame, not between the two panels.</figcaption></figure>